package skill

// TraceJankQueryContract is shared by trace exploration and the tool schema.
// It is guidance for typed queries, not a classifier over request prose.
const TraceJankQueryContract = "JANK MARKERS: jank_event_sync markers report start_ts/end_ts in native nanoseconds, jank_frames (2 means a stall of two frames), and appid. For numeric questions use event_search with event_field_filters, for example [{\"field\":\"jank_frames\",\"op\":\"gte\",\"value\":\"2\"}]; add {\"field\":\"appid\",\"op\":\"eq\",\"value\":\"27599\"} for one app. Conditions are ANDed; eq/ne/gt/gte/lt/lte support equality, thresholds and ranges. These match validated numeric fields, not text patterns or regex. Use quoted decimal integers to preserve nanosecond precision. appid is the marker's application identifier, not the emitter TID. Explicit pid filters the emitter TID; thread keeps its existing name/text matching and is not identity proof. Numeric field queries do not inherit an implicit target-thread filter. time_start/time_end select trace header timestamps in seconds; start_ts/end_ts field conditions select the native payload clock in nanoseconds. Never assume those clocks agree or infer an offset from proximity. Preserve the native fields, reporting timestamp and physical source line in the answer. For all/count questions distinguish matched_total from emitted rows and inspect coverage/truncation before claiming completeness; continue with the same filters when paging. Explain these as total matches, shown records and search scope in user-facing language. A marker locates a reported symptom, not its cause. Before scheduler/causal drilldown, establish the target thread and time-domain mapping from independent evidence; retain explicit user windows and existing Trace supplementation. Only proven chain evidence supplies root causes; nearby work remains background."
